+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:33:33 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH 5/6] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: decode the Dolby Vision profile
+ 7 enhancement layer
+
+A single-track Dolby Vision profile 7 stream carries its enhancement
+layer as type 63 NAL units inside the base layer's access units. Full
+enhancement layer (FEL) pictures are wrong without it.
+
+When the Dolby Vision tunnel can be used, CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME splits
+each packet into its layers, decodes the enhancement layer with a second
+hardware decoder and pairs the layers' pictures by display time, with
+libpi_engine's input glue. A buffer then carries both frames, and the
+tunnel renders the enhancement layer where the picture's RPU needs it.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
